Done. Here's what I built:

What changed: When a user quits yoyo (Ctrl-D or `/quit`), the exit summary now shows a compact colored diff of session changes — not just file names.

**Implementation:**

1. `truncate_diff_lines(diff, max_lines)` — new helper that truncates a diff to at most N lines, appending a dim overflow hint like … and 15 more lines (use /changes --diff to see all). Preserves ANSI color codes in kept lines.

2. `format_exit_summary()` — after the "Files changed" line, if not in quiet mode (is_quiet()), collects git diffs via the existing collect_diffs() function and appends a truncated (15 lines max) colored diff.

3. Guards:
   • Skipped in quiet/`--print mode (is_quiet()`)
   • Skipped when diff is empty (already-committed changes won't show in git diff)

4. 5 new tests covering: empty input, shorter-than-max, exact-max, over-max with overflow hint, and ANSI preservation.
